```

**Compiler note:** The compiler used to build the C++ extension must be *ABI-compatible* with the compiler PyTorch was built with. In practice: GCC version 4.9+ on Linux (default on Ubuntu 16.04+); on MacOS, use clang (no ABI versioning issues). Worst case: build PyTorch from source with your compiler and build the extension with that same compiler.

---

## 10. Performance Comparison Numbers (from the tutorial)

| Implementation | Forward | Backward |
|---|---|---|
| Pure Python/PyTorch (CPU) | 506.480 us | 444.694 us |
| C++/ATen (CPU) | 349.335 us | 443.523 us |
