## 9. Build / Install Commands

Directory structure:

```
pytorch/
  lltm-extension/
    lltm.cpp
    setup.py
```

Build and install command:

```
python setup.py install
```

Importing the extension (be sure to `import torch` first so the dynamic linker resolves symbols):

```python
In [1]: import torch
In [2]: import lltm_cpp
In [3]: lltm_cpp.forward
Out[3]: <function lltm.PyCapsule.forward>
```

Calling `help()` shows the signature:

```
In[4] help(lltm_cpp.forward)
forward(...) method of builtins.PyCapsule instance
    forward(arg0: torch::Tensor, arg1: torch::Tensor, arg2: torch::Tensor, arg3: torch::Tensor, arg4: torch::Tensor) -> List[torch::Tensor]

    LLTM forward
```

**Compiler note:** The compiler used to build the C++ extension must be *ABI-compatible* with the compiler PyTorch was built with. In practice: GCC version 4.9+ on Linux (default on Ubuntu 16.04+); on MacOS, use clang (no ABI versioning issues). Worst case: build PyTorch from source with your compiler and build the extension with that same compiler.

